   821	**Has anyone beaten c = 1 rigorously (1992–2026)?** To our knowledge, no. Codex pcest_1 and pcest_2 and
   822	the Opus literature critic (§7) all searched. Neither found a rigorous algorithm factoring every N in L[1/2, c] with c < 1. The
   823	rigorous record remains Lenstra–Pomerance 1992 (JAMS 5, 483–516).
   824	- Related results are either heuristic (NFS; Stange 2022) or concern other problems:
   825	  - Kleinjung–Wesolowski: discrete logarithms in finite fields of fixed characteristic (JAMS 35, 2022).
   826	  - de Boer–Pellet-Mary–Wesolowski (arXiv 2512.01588): ERH, class and unit groups.
   827	- Under GRH the best rigorous constant is also c = 1: Seysen and A. K. Lenstra's class-group method,
   828	  whose GRH dependence Lenstra–Pomerance removed. We know of no c < 1 under a standard hypothesis.
   829	- Lee–Venkatesan (J. Number Theory 187 (2018) 92–159) produce congruences in L[1/3], but their
   830	  factoring conclusion is
   831	  conditional on their Conjecture 7.1.
   832	- This is a search result, not a certification.
