   289	    algebra costs L[1/2, 2a].
   290	  - For θ < 1 the optimum is at a = θ/√2, giving c = (1+θ)/√2.
   291	  - Without the shape cost, c would be √(2θ). The first version claimed that, but it is not achievable
   292	    with a rigorous shape test at fixed k.
   293	  - Recursive variant: use this algorithm itself as the shape test, assuming D_k at all scales. The
   294	    fixed point c = a + c/√2 with θ/(2a) ≤ c − a gives c = √((1+√2)θ).
   295	- *Sizes.*
