   297	  - The rational cofactor is (a − bm)/ℓ = N^{s − 1/(4k) + o(1)}.
   298	  - F(a, b) = N^{s + h + d/(4k) + o(1)}, where H = N^h is the coefficient height of R_A.
   299	  - The level-½ condition |a − bm| ≤ |F|^{1/2−η} is used by FM (§4). It needs h > s − (d−2)/(4k) + 2η.
   300	  - Adding the rational and algebraic sizes gives θ(d,k) + O(η).
   301	- θ(d,k) ↓ 3s as k → ∞.
   302	  - The displayed limits are infima over growing *fixed* k (codex); they are not attained at any
   303	    finite k. Limits of c = (1+θ)/√2: d = 7: 0.973; d = 9: 0.920 (0.923 at k = 50); d = 11: 0.884; d = 19: 0.814;
   304	    d → ∞: 1/√2.
   305	  - Recursive variant: 0.851 at d = 9.
   306	  - All numbers were checked numerically by us and by both proof critics.
   307	
   308	**Prop H (the bounded-k dilemma) [proved arithmetic].** With k large primes per split,
   309	Pr[all in G_A] ≈ g_A^{k}.
   310	- **Horn 1: an L^{o(1)} rigorous shape test.** HECM costs L_v[2/3] for primes ≤ v. This is L^{o(1)} iff
   311	  log v = o((log N)^{3/4}(log log N)^{1/4}), which forces k ≥ (log N)^{1/4−o(1)}.
   312	  - Then g_A, and so every averaged estimate, must be accurate to exp(−o((log N)^{1/4}(log log N)^{1/2}))
   313	    (B3).
   314	  - LV-type goodness only gives L^{o(1)} losses in the exponent.
   315	  - lemmaM's B1 = exp((log N)^{3/4}) sits on this horn.
   316	- **Horn 2: bounded k.** g_A = L^{−o(1)} suffices, but every shape test is a factorisation of
   317	  √N-size integers into N^{Θ(1)}-size primes.
   318	  - The best *available* rigorous test is Lenstra–Pomerance, at L_N[1/2, 1/√2].
   319	  - This is an upper bound. No lower bound shows that every rigorous shape test must pay it (codex
   320	    wording fix).
   321	- **Growing k (codex).** Let T = √(log N log log N). Interpolating between the horns requires
   322	  k·log log N = o(T) and k·log(1/γ) = o(T). Writing γ = L^{−o(1)} does not by itself give the second
   323	  condition.
   324	- Either way something is paid. Horn 2 still allows c < 1 conditionally, (1+θ)/√2. But Design V
   325	  (√(2/3)) is better unless d ≥ 19.
