   181	## 3. Lemma W (the forced residue becomes spread)
   182	
   183	**Cited.**
   184	- **(BT)** Montgomery–Vaughan (Mathematika 20 (1973) 119–134, Thm 2): for 1 ≤ q < x and (a, q) = 1,
   185	  π(x; q, a) ≤ 2x/(φ(q) log(x/q)).
   186	- **(PNT)** π(2W) − π(W) ≥ W/(2 log W) for W ≥ W₀.
   187	
   188	**Lemma W [proved].** For every t ∈ [1, 2MV_max] and every a ∈ Z,
   189	  Pr_w[w ≡ a (mod t)] ≤ C_W/φ(t),  with C_W := 24/η₀,
   190	for all N ≥ N₀(d, k, σ, η₀).
   191	
   192	*Proof.*
   193	- If (a, t) > 1 the probability is 0, since w > t is prime.
   194	- Otherwise #{w ∈ (W, 2W] prime : w ≡ a (mod t)} ≤ π(2W; t, a) ≤ 4W/(φ(t) log(2W/t)).
   195	- Divide by W/(2 log W). This gives ≤ 8 log W/(φ(t) log(2W/t)).
   196	- Now log W ≤ (s + 1/(4k) + η₀) log N ≤ log N. Since 2MV_max ≤ N^{s+1/(4k)}L^{O(1)},
   197	  log(2W/t) ≥ (η₀/2) log N − O(Λ) ≥ (η₀/3) log N. ∎
   198	(Exact toy check: `bt_ratio`, `test_brun_titchmarsh_ratio`.)
