   201	  E_w Φ(r₀) ≤ (C_W/φ(t)) Σ_{c ∈ (Z/t)^×} Φ(c).
   202	This holds for any (ℓ, P, g) with gcd(G(P), N) = 1, in particular whenever Y_P = 1. ∎
   203	
   204	This replaces the large-values problem (critic piece (ii)). The bound is uniform in the rational data,
   205	so the rational weights can be summed separately (§5, Step 5).
   206	
   207	## 4. Theorem BDH_fam (critic piece (i), all-residue, at precision L^{o(1)})
   208	
   209	**Notation.**
   210	- X* := X_F^max = C′_d MH V_max^d. It is common to all ℓ ∈ J and dominates every window below.

